      "content": "yeah those are valid points. the issue is the decision is pretty much final—the budget for the agent framework was cut and we're just transitioning to the lambda setup for everything.\n\ni'm looking at the code for the `agent_core/runtime.py` deletion part now. if we just strip out the orchestrator and the loop, do you think there's any way to keep the core logic running without the heavy framework, or is it basically a clean break? i'm trying to see if we can salvage any of the reasoning modules or if they're too tied to the agent loop.",
      "source": "evaluator"
